    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8552A\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the county of Nassau to alienate certain lands used\nas parklands to enable the Port Washington Water District to construct,\nmaintain and operate a water treatment facility\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation authorizes the alienation of certain parklands for the\nconstruction and maintenance of a new water treatment facility aimed at\ntreating emerging contaminants.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Authorizes Nassau County to discontinue the lands described\nfurther in this legislation as parklands for the creation and mainte-\nnance of a water treatment facility.\n\nSection 2: Requires that authorization is only granted if Nassau County\ndedicates an amount equal to or greater than the fair market value of\nthe parklands being discontinued for funding for capital improvements,\nto existing park and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 3: Contains the description of the parklands seeking to be\nalienated.\n\nSection 4: States that the discontinuation of parklands shall not occur\nuntil the Secretary of the Interior signs off on conditions for alien-\nation are met.\n\nSection 5: States that lands described in Section 3 shall revert back to\nparklands once they are done being used for the express purpose of this\nact.\n\nSection 6: Effective Date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis parkland alienation bill is necessary for the construction of a new\nwater treatment facility to address the needs of area residents as it\npertains to emerging contaminants. Water quality is of critical impor-\ntance for area residents and this legislation is necessary to ensure\nthat they are protected against various emerging contaminants.  In seek-\ning to protect residents against harmful chemicals in their drinking\nwater, a new water treatment plant is necessary.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  New Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day.\n",
